CPU alloc-only buffer type for the MoE-SSD (LES) model load path.

The pinned fork (tc-mb/llama.cpp-omni @ 96bbf617) can only load the stripped
`-les` MiniCPM-V 4.7 GGUF if the backend registry answers the
"ggml_backend_dev_buffer_type_alloc_only" lookup: llama_model synthesizes the
stripped routed-expert tensors from the experts manifest and must place them
on a buffer type that is NOT the device default, because load_tensors wraps
default-buft tensors into the (read-only) mmap of the model file while expert
content is written at runtime by preadv from the experts pack.

At the pin, only the Metal backend implements that lookup (it hands out its
"mapped" buffer type: a distinct instance with ordinary allocations). The
CPU backend exports no such proc, so llama_model_load_from_file throws
"backend has no alloc-only buft" and returns null on Android (build 6;
build 5 died one check earlier, on the slot-bank contract).

This patch mirrors the Metal semantics for CPU:
- ggml-backend.cpp gains ggml_backend_cpu_buffer_type_alloc_only(): a second
  CPU buffer type instance (name "CPU_AllocOnly") whose iface is exactly the
  default CPU one (ggml_aligned_malloc host memory, TENSOR_ALIGNMENT,
  is_host=true), defined next to the existing "CPU_Mapped" precedent.
- ggml-cpu.cpp answers "ggml_backend_dev_buffer_type_alloc_only" in
  ggml_backend_cpu_get_proc_address with a reg-level wrapper honoring the
  size_t device-index argument (CPU registry has one device; out-of-range
  returns nullptr, like Metal's bounds check).

Applied to the fetched fork by scripts/prepare_v47.py; the vendored checkout
is never edited by hand. No behavior changes for any other buffer type.

